# ::bentoo's Rust 1.99.1 mirror (d1b669163, 2026-10-19) is invisible to every
# ::gentoo Rust consumer. Those ebuilds read ::gentoo's rust.eclass, whose slot
# table stops at 1.99.0; ::bentoo's forked eclass, which adds the 1.99.1 row,
# shadows only ::bentoo's own ebuilds (its header says so). An unslotted
# dev-lang/rust-bin (kits/core/portage) then resolves to 1.99.1, and
# dev-vcs/git-2.56.0-r1 dies in pkg_setup with "No Rust matching requirements
# (>= 1.90.0) found installed!" -- the pin proof of ::gentoo 20261101 +
# ::bentoo 1d98e5f on bentoo-lab, 2026-11-09, toolbox stage base, 253/504.
#
# Masked here, not in ::bentoo, so the overlay pin stays the last commit of the
# snapshot's day. ::gentoo 20261101 carries rust, rust-bin and rust-common
# 1.99.0, so this mask leaves a candidate for each.
# Remove it once the pinned ::gentoo rust.eclass lists 1.99.1 (or ::bentoo
# drops the mirror).
=dev-lang/rust-1.99.1::bentoo
=dev-lang/rust-bin-1.99.1::bentoo
=dev-lang/rust-common-1.99.1::bentoo
